  (62, 'Sweet annie', 'Artemisia annua', 10, 'Spice', 0, 0, NULL, 'Artemisia annua', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Sweet annie.jpg', 'አርተሚዚያ', 'sweet-annie', 'croptype-818791209390', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (63, 'Citronella grass', 'Cymbopogon winteranius', 10, 'Spice', 0, 0, NULL, 'Cymbopogon winteranius', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Citronella grass.jpg', 'የናርዶስ ሳር', 'citronella-grass', 'croptype-089152903238', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (64, 'Pyrethrum', 'Chrysanthemum cinerariaefolium', 10, 'Spice', 0, 0, NULL, 'Chrysanthemum cinerariaefolium', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Pyrethrum.jpg', 'ፓይረትረም', 'pyrethrum', 'croptype-392924463876', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (65, 'Cumin', 'Nigella sativa', NULL, 'Spice', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'UNRESOLVED', 'UNRESOLVED', 'UNRESOLVED'),
  (66, 'Lemmon grass', 'Cymbopogon citratus (DC) Stapf)', 10, 'Can be used as carminative, insect repellant and widely  used as herbal tea. It has a remedial properties and is used to treat  bronchitis, sinusitis, cold, fever, malaria, hemorrhoids, toothache, baby  oil, massage oil, ointment for body, oil for rheumatism, oil for beauty  mask, herbal baths, sop and candle making industries and herbal  cooking‟s', 0, 0, NULL, 'Cymbopogon citratus (DC) Stapf', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Lemon grass.jpg', 'ሎሚ ሳር', 'lemon-grass', 'croptype-943756684079', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'REVIEWED_TYPE_ALIAS', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (67, 'Speare mint', 'Mentha spicata L.', 10, 'Among mint species, spearmint (Mentha spicata L.) is considered industrial crop as it is a source of essential oils  enriched in certain monoterpenes like carvol, dihydrocarveole,  dihydrocarveylacetate, menthol, menthone, caryophyllene, terpineol  and cubebene which is widely used in food, flavor, cosmetic and  pharmaceutical industries.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Mentha spicata L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Spearmint.jpg', 'ናና', 'spearmint', 'croptype-670738359780', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'REVIEWED_TYPE_ALIAS', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (68, 'Spanish mint', 'Mentha spicata ''Spanish Pointed''', 10, 'A full-flavored mint use Spanish mint in tea,  soups, stirs fry, salads and more. It is used in teas, beverages, jellies,  syrups, ice creams, confections, chutneys.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Mentha spicata ''Spanish pointed''', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Spanish mint.jpg', 'ናና', 'spanish-mint', 'croptype-536373285121', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (69, 'African marigold', 'Tagetes erecta L.', 10, 'African marigold (Tagetes erecta L.) is a  widely cultivated as bedding plants, loose flower, perfume, natural  color, pigments, carotinoids, insect and nematodes repellents, nutrient  supplement for poultry feed.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Tagetes erecta L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/African marigold.jpg', NULL, 'african-marigold', 'croptype-818789108822', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (70, 'Rose Scented Geranium', 'Pelargonium graveolens L. Herit', 10, 'The essential oil has wide-ranging uses in flavor and fragrance  industries, aromatherapy, cosmetic industries, food and pharmaceutical  industries.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Pelargonium graveolens L. Herit', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/geranium.webp', NULL, 'geranium', 'croptype-423946881555', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'REVIEWED_TYPE_ALIAS', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (71, 'Chamomile', 'Matricaria chamomilla L.', 10, 'It is a well-known aromatic and medicinal  plant often referred to as the “star among medicinal species”.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Matricaria chamomilla L.', 'DZARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Chamomile.jpg', 'ከሞሜላ', 'chamomile', 'croptype-383110700217', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (72, 'Lemon verbena', 'Aloysia triphylla L.', 10, 'The leaves of lemon verbena are the most economical part of the plant  that can be used anywhere to add a lemony taste in salads, tea, milk, ice  creams and jellies.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Aloysia triphylla L.', 'WGARC', 3, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Lemon verbena.jpg', 'ሎሚናት', 'lemon-verbena', 'croptype-225922814390', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (73, 'Stevia', 'Stevia rebaudiana Bertoni L.', 10, 'It is being cultivated  in Japan, Taiwan, Philippines, Hawaii, Malaysia and overall South  America for food and pharmaceutical products. The property of the  species that called attention to the plant was the intense sweet tests of  the leaves and aqueous extracts.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Stevia rebaudiana Bertoni L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/stevia.webp', 'ስቴቪያ', 'stevia', 'croptype-310780138063', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (74, 'Hibiscus', 'Hibiscus subdariffa L.', 10, 'Many parts of the plant are of value  with the leaves, seeds and calyces widely used as either food or drug.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Hibiscus subdariffa L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Hibiscus.jpg', 'ከርከዴ', 'hibiscus', 'croptype-029136077947', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (75, 'Lavender', 'Lavandula angustifolia L.', 10, 'Lavender is a perennial, bushy shrub  growing 0,3 to 1,2 m high and the aromatic evergreen leaves are  completely opposite and up to 5 cm long. It produces essential oil and  the parts used for essential oil distillation are the flowers and leaves.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Lavandula angustifolia L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Lavender.jpg', NULL, 'lavender', 'croptype-041770391216', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (76, 'Majoram/Oregano', 'Origanum vulgaris L.', 10, 'The  use of oregano as medicinal plant is believed to be due to biological  properties of p-cymene and carvacrol. The fresh leaves and dried herb  of oregano as well as essential oil are used medicinally.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Origannum vulgaris L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Majoram.jpg', NULL, 'majoram-oregano', 'croptype-131068677144', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'REVIEWED_TYPE_ALIAS', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (77, 'Sage', 'Salvia officinalis L.', 10, 'Essential oil of sage is applied in the treatment of a range of diseases  and has been shown to possess antimicrobial, viricidal, cytotoxic,  antimutagenic and antifungal activities.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Saliva officinalis L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Sage.jpg', NULL, 'sage', 'croptype-146185367281', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (78, 'Vanilla', 'Vanilla planifolia', 10, 'Popular flavoring substance called vanillin, which is mainly used in  flavoring of different food and beverages, and in cosmetics and  perfumery industry, condiments and oleoresin.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Vanilla planifolia', 'TNSRC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Vanilla.jpg', 'ቫኒላ', 'vanilla', 'croptype-649571398221', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (79, 'Basil', 'Ocimum basilicum L.', 10, 'Basil has been extensively utilized  in food as a flavoring agent, and in perfumery and medical industries', 0, 0, NULL, 'Ocimum basilicum L.', 'WGARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/basil.jpg', NULL, 'basil', 'croptype-546893412353', 'spices-condiments-medicinal-aromatic', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (80, 'Banana', 'Musa paradisiaca var. sapiertum', 5, 'There are two types of banana, namely dessert and cooking types.  Banana flowers in about 9-12 months and the fruits mature in about 3-4  months. Hence the crop would be ready for harvest in 12 - 16 months  after planting depending on the variety. The yield is roughly 30 - 40  tons/ha.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Musa paradisiaca var. sapiertum', 'MARC', 2, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Banana.jpg', 'ሙዝ', 'banana', 'croptype-768903809650', 'fruit-and-vegetables', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (81, 'Mango', 'Mangifera indica L.', 5, 'Mango is a fruit of frost free tropical  and warmer sub-tropical climates. Nowadays it is produced more than  any other fruit crop around the world.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Mangifera indica L.', 'MARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Mango.jpg', 'ማንጎ', 'mango', 'croptype-899576185560', 'fruit-and-vegetables', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (82, 'Pineapple', 'Ananas comosus', 5, 'Pineapple is an herbaceous short-lived perennial plant which  grows to 1.0 to 1.5 meters tall. The plant only produces one fruit and  then dies. Commercially suckers that appear around the base are  cultivated', 0, 0, NULL, 'Ananas comosus', 'JARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Pineapple.jpg', 'አናናስ', 'pineapple', 'croptype-872170508253', 'fruit-and-vegetables', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (83, 'Wine grape', 'Vitis vinifera', 5, 'Grape vines (Vitis vinifera) belong to the genus Vitis. The Genus  includes several species which produce palatable fruits and byproducts, primarily wine. Grapes can be in the form of table grapes and  raisins or dried grapes which are equally important in the international  market.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Vitis vinifera', 'DZARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Wine grape.jpg', 'ወይን', 'wine-grape', 'croptype-568102620935', 'fruit-and-vegetables', 'Ethiopian grape wine represents a growing and promising segment of the country’s agricultural and agro-processing sector. Produced mainly from grapes cultivated in highland and Rift Valley areas, Ethiopian grape wine reflects the country’s diverse agro-ecological conditions, characterized by abundant sunshine, moderate temperatures, and suitable altitudes that favor grape quality and sugar accumulation. The wine industry in Ethiopia combines traditional agricultural practices with modern viticulture and winemaking technologies. Locally produced wines are typically made from both introduced and adapted grape varieties, resulting in wines that range from light and fruity to fuller-bodied styles. Ethiopian grape wines often exhibit fresh acidity, mild tannins, and pleasant aromas, making them suitable for local consumption and emerging regional markets. Beyond its beverage value, grape wine production contributes to employment creation, value addition, and income diversification for farmers and agro-industries. The sector also supports the development of associated industries such as glass manufacturing, packaging, and tourism. With continued investment in improved varieties, vineyard management, and quality control, Ethiopian grape wine has strong potential to enhance domestic supply and gradually compete in international niche markets. Overall, Ethiopian grape wine symbolizes the country’s evolving capacity to transform agricultural produce into high-value products while promoting agro-industrial development and economic growth.', 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
  (84, 'Avocado', 'Persea americana M.

Avocados were first seen in the United States in the early 1800''s.
California is currently the largest producer of avocados stateside. There
are more than 80 varieties, with the "Hass" variety dominating the crop
share. A single mature avocado tree can produce more than 400 pieces
of fruit in a year.Avocados are loaded with nutrients such as dietary fiber, vitamin B6,
vitamin C, vitamin E, potassium, magnesium, and folate. They''re also
cholesterol and sodium free.', 6, 'Avocados are loaded with nutrients such as dietary fiber, vitamin B6,  vitamin C, vitamin E, potassium, magnesium, and folate. They''re also  cholesterol and sodium free. Avocados contain 60% more potassium  per ounce than bananas. This fruit is an excellent source of  monounsaturated fat.', 0, 0, 2, 'Persea americana M.', 'MARC', 2, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Avocado.jpg', 'አቮካዶ', 'avocado', 'croptype-928367285259', 'fruit-and-vegetables', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG'),
  (85, 'Date palm', 'Phoenix dactylifera L', 5, 'Date Palm plays an  important nutritional, economical, religion, cultural and ecological role  in desert and semi desert agro-ecologies of Ethiopia. It is also  historically known that people inhibiting in deserts live on dates and  milk without suffering any nutritional problem.', 0, 0, NULL, 'Phoenix dactylifera L.', 'WARC', 0, 'http://196.191.93.34/moa-portal/cropopen/varieites/crops/Date palm.jpg', NULL, 'date-palm', 'croptype-710600158551', 'fruit-and-vegetables', NULL, 'SQL_CROP_CATALOG', 'SQL_CROP_VARIETY', 'EXACT_NORMALIZED_NAME', 'MATCHED', 'WORKBOOK_TAXONOMY_MAPPING'),
